    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Nutrition</span> is the process by which organisms obtain and use food for energy, growth, and repair. Plants are autotrophs (make their own food through photosynthesis), while animals are heterotrophs (obtain food by consuming other organisms).</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Photosynthesis (Plant Nutrition)</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">6CO₂ + 6H₂O + light energy → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂</p><ul class=\"learn-list\"><li>Occurs in chloroplasts, in the grana (light reactions) and stroma (dark reactions/Calvin cycle)</li><li>Chlorophyll absorbs red and blue light; reflects green (hence leaves appear green)</li><li>Factors affecting rate: light intensity, CO₂ concentration, temperature, water availability</li><li>Light reactions: water photolysis, ATP and NADPH production, O₂ released</li><li>Dark reactions (Calvin cycle): CO₂ fixed using ATP and NADPH to produce glucose</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Mineral Nutrition in Plants</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Mineral</th><th>Function</th><th>Deficiency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nitrogen (N)</td><td>Amino acids, proteins, nucleic acids</td><td>Stunted growth, yellowing (chlorosis)</td></tr><tr><td>Phosphorus (P)</td><td>DNA, ATP, cell membranes</td><td>Purple leaves, poor root growth</td></tr><tr><td>Potassium (K)</td><td>Enzyme activation, stomatal control</td><td>Brown leaf margins, wilting</td></tr><tr><td>Magnesium (Mg)</td><td>Central atom of chlorophyll</td><td>Yellowing between veins (interveinal chlorosis)</td></tr><tr><td>Iron (Fe)</td><td>Chlorophyll synthesis</td><td>Yellowing of young leaves</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Animal Nutrition</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Classes of food: carbohydrates (energy), proteins (growth and repair), fats/lipids (energy store, insulation), vitamins (metabolic regulation), minerals (body building), water (solvent, transport, cooling).</p><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Digestion</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Mechanical digestion (physical breakdown) + chemical digestion (enzyme action). Key enzymes: amylase (starch→maltose), protease/pepsin (protein→peptides), lipase (fat→fatty acids + glycerol).</p><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span><strong>Photosynthesis:</strong> Light reactions in grana (thylakoids). Dark reactions in stroma (Calvin cycle). O₂ released from water (not CO₂).</div><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span><strong>Summary:</strong> Photosynthesis: 6CO₂+6H₂O+light→C₆H₁₂O₆+6O₂. Limiting factors: light, CO₂, temp. Nitrogen deficiency → chlorosis. Digestion: amylase→starch, pepsin→protein, lipase→fat.</div>",
