    "contentHTML": "<div class=\"learn-intro\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Pollution</span> is the introduction of harmful substances or energy into the environment. <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Conservation</span> is the management and protection of natural resources and biodiversity for present and future generations.</div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Types and Effects of Pollution</h3><div class=\"learn-table-wrap\"><table class=\"learn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Examples</th><th>Effects</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Air pollution</td><td>SO₂, NOₓ, CO, particulates, CFCs</td><td>Acid rain, respiratory disease, ozone depletion, global warming</td></tr><tr><td>Water pollution</td><td>Sewage, fertilisers, oil spills, heavy metals</td><td>Eutrophication, disease, death of aquatic life, bioaccumulation</td></tr><tr><td>Soil pollution</td><td>Pesticides, heavy metals, oil spills</td><td>Reduced soil fertility, food chain contamination</td></tr><tr><td>Noise pollution</td><td>Industrial noise, traffic</td><td>Hearing loss, stress, sleep disturbance</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Biodiversity and Its Importance</h3><ul class=\"learn-list\"><li>Biodiversity = variety of living organisms in an ecosystem</li><li>Importance: ecosystem services (clean water, O₂ production, pollination, soil formation), food security, medicinal plants, aesthetic value</li><li>Threats: habitat destruction, overexploitation, pollution, invasive species, climate change</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Conservation Strategies</h3><ul class=\"learn-list\"><li><strong>In-situ conservation:</strong> protection in natural habitat (game reserves, national parks, biosphere reserves, marine reserves)</li><li><strong>Ex-situ conservation:</strong> protection outside natural habitat (zoos, botanical gardens, seed banks, captive breeding)</li><li>Afforestation, reforestation, sustainable agriculture, waste management</li></ul><h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Deforestation and Its Effects</h3><p class=\"learn-p\">Effects: loss of biodiversity, soil erosion, flooding, climate change (less CO₂ absorbed), disruption of water cycle, displacement of communities.</p><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span><strong>In-situ vs Ex-situ:</strong> In-situ = in natural habitat (national parks). Ex-situ = outside habitat (zoos, seed banks). In-situ is preferred — preserves ecological interactions.</div><div class=\"learn-tip-box\"><span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span><strong>Summary:</strong> Pollution types: air (SO₂, CFCs), water (sewage, fertilisers), soil (pesticides). Biodiversity: threatened by deforestation, pollution. Conservation: in-situ (national parks) or ex-situ (zoos, seed banks).</div>",
